    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-8565",
      "problem": "Given $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace,$ compute $P(X \\geq 9).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/edd21e889880a17bf01ba4742986e07434e887664a34db1c86a427ce795271fe.svg)\n\nHere, we have $X \\sim U \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace,$ and the set $S = \\left\\lbrace 5, 6, 7, \\ldots, 14 \\right\\rbrace$ has $|S|=14 - 5 + 1 = 10$ items. So, we have\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14268989/assets/d178ec392849db8cbb830784d1302fa01d590999a79b7641ee4baa4452363bed.svg)\n\nIn $S,$ the items that satisfy $X \\geq 9$ are $9, 10, 11, \\ldots , 14.$ There are $14 - 9 + 1 = 6$ of these items. Therefore,\n\n$$\nP(X \\geq 9) = 6 \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{10} = \\dfrac{3}{5}.\n$$",
